    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Oozing with architectural character and rich in period detail, no.75 Philipsburgh Avenue, Fairview is a superb example of elegant Edwardian design. This handsome red-brick three-bedroom residence extends to approximately 112m2 / 1,206 sqft and retains some lovely original features including fireplaces, floorboards, high ceilings and ornate plaster cornicing.\r\n\r\nA bright and inviting entrance hall welcomes you on arrival and leads to nicely proportioned interconnecting reception rooms. The front reception room features an original fireplace and generous bay window. A kitchen/dining space is positioned just off the rear reception room and is well-appointed with contemporary style units and a set of French doors that open out to the garden.  \r\n\r\nUpstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms together with a beautifully upgraded family bathroom positioned on the first-floor return. The front-facing principal bedroom is particularly spacious and spans right across the full width of the house. The attic bedroom also lends itself perfectly as a home office and features a dormer window that fills the space with natural light.\r\n\r\nOutside, the railed front garden complements the charming red-brick streetscape synonymous with this popular residential address. To the rear, the neatly maintained south-west facing garden is a wonderful sun trap and includes a brick-fronted garden shed with access to a gated ‘residents-only’ rear laneway.\r\n\r\nResidents of Fairview enjoy an exceptional range of amenities on their doorstep, including an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, bars, supermarkets and independent retailers. Fairview Park and Clontarf’s seafront promenade are both within easy reach, offering superb recreational amenities nearby. The area is exceptionally well connected with numerous bus routes, Clontarf Road DART Station, Connolly Station and the LUAS all close at hand. The property is also within comfortable walking distance of the city centre, IFSC, East Point Business Park and Dublin’s thriving Docklands."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
        "SortOrder": 2,
        "Content": "Entrance Porch - \r\nRecessed porch with tiled floor. \r\n\r\nEntrance Hall - 3.85m x 1.13m \r\nVarnised floorboards, recessed alcove, dado rail and ceiling cornice. \r\n\r\nReception Room 1 - 3.29m x 3.31m \r\nFront-facing living room with generous bay window and original cast-iron firplace with tiled inset and surround. Ceiling cornice and picture rail. \r\n\r\nReception Room 2 - 3.24m x 3.72m \r\nCeiling cornice and centre rose, picture rail, radiator cover and natural sisal carpet. \r\n\r\nKitchen - 3.24m x 2.53m \r\nOpen plan kitchen/dining space with contemporary style units and solid wood countertop. \r\n\r\nDining Room - 3.47m x 2.05m \r\nOpen plan kitchen/dining space with tiled floor, velux roof light and french door opening to garden. \r\n\r\nFirst Floor Landing - \r\nNatural sisal carpet flooring. \r\n\r\nBedroom 1 - 3.37m x 4.96m \r\nSpacious master bedroom with feature cast-iron fireplace and varnished floorboards. Ceiling cornice. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2 - 3.33m x 3.29m \r\nDouble size bedroom with varnished floorboards. \r\n\r\nBathroom - 1.85m x 2.39m \r\nRemodelled family bathroom with new suite and tiling. Bath with shower screen and electric shower, whb and seperate wc. \r\n\r\nHot Press - \r\n\r\n\r\nSecond Floor Landing - \r\nNatural sisal carpet flooring. \r\n\r\nBedroom 3 - 4.24m x 3.47m \r\nDouble size bedroom with dormer window and varnished floorboards. Downlighting. \r\n\r\nUnder Eave Storage - \r\n\r\n\r\n"
      },
